  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Itaconic Anhydride interacts with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, through a series of target interactions involving EDD domain proteins. The drug is implicated in targeting the DegV family of EDD domain proteins, which are subsequently targeted by other compounds such as Androstanedione and RA-Xii. These compounds, in turn, are linked to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, indicating a possible pathway where Itaconic Anhydride may modulate the activity of this enzyme. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and plausible relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential role for Itaconic Anhydride in influencing the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, possibly through the inhibition of EDD domain proteins that are downstream targets of the drug. The integration of multiple pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction network, but the core mechanism remains consistent across the evidence.",
